1
00:04:53,076 --> 00:04:59,076
Expect The Savage. The Sensual. The Shocking. The Sad. The
Powerful. The Shameful. Expect The Truth.

2
00:09:46,153 --> 00:09:52,153
Mandingo is a romance, drama, history film directed by Richard Fleischer.

3
00:14:39,230 --> 00:14:45,230
Warren Maxwell, the owner of a run-down plantation, pressures his son,
Hammond, to marry and produce an heir to inherit the plantation.

4
00:19:32,307 --> 00:19:38,307
Hammond settles on his own cousin, Blanche, but purchases a
sex slave when he returns from the honeymoon.

5
00:24:25,384 --> 00:24:31,384
He also buys his father a new Mandingo slave named Mede
to breed and train as a prize-fighter.

6
00:29:18,461 --> 00:29:24,461
Hammond Maxwell, played by Perry King.

7
00:34:11,538 --> 00:34:17,538
Warren Maxwell, played by James Mason.

8
00:39:04,615 --> 00:39:10,615
Blanche Woodford Maxwell, played by Susan George.

9
00:43:57,692 --> 00:44:03,692
Mede (Ganymede), played by Ken Norton.

10
00:48:50,769 --> 00:48:56,769
Agamemnon, played by Richard Ward.

11
00:53:43,846 --> 00:53:49,846
Ellen, played by Brenda Sykes.

12
00:58:36,923 --> 00:58:42,923
Mandingo is a 1975 American historical melodrama film focusing on
the Atlantic slave trade in the Antebellum South.

13
01:03:30,000 --> 01:03:36,000
The film's title refers to the Mandinka people, who are referred to as
"Mandingos", and described as being good slaves for fighting matches.

14
01:08:23,076 --> 01:08:29,076
The word is also used as a pejorative to describe a hypersexual Black man.

15
01:13:16,153 --> 01:13:22,153
Produced by Dino De Laurentiis for Paramount Pictures, the
film was directed by Richard Fleischer.

16
01:18:09,230 --> 01:18:15,230
The screenplay, by Norman Wexler, was adapted from the 1957 novel Mandingo by Kyle Onstott,
and the 1961 play Mandingo by Jack Kirkland (which is derived from the novel).

17
01:23:02,307 --> 01:23:08,307
The film stars Perry King as Hammond, the son of cruel
slave owner Warren Maxwell (James Mason).

18
01:27:55,384 --> 01:28:01,384
Hammond is known to have sex with female slaves on his father's plantation, and his father
orders him to marry a white woman to produce grandchildren with no black ancestry.

19
01:32:48,461 --> 01:32:54,461
Hammond marries Blanche (Susan George), his cousin, who becomes jealous that he pays more attention to his black lover Ellen (Brenda Sykes)
than to his wife, leading Blanche to force the Mandingo fighting slave Mede (Ken Norton) into a sexual relationship with her.

20
01:37:41,538 --> 01:37:47,538
Mandingo received negative reviews upon release.

21
01:42:34,615 --> 01:42:40,615
However, retrospectively, the film's reception became much more favorable.

22
01:47:27,692 --> 01:47:33,692
It has been variously seen as a big-budget exploitation film made by a major studio, a serious film about American
slavery, examining historical horrors committed against African Americans, or as a work of camp.

23
01:52:20,769 --> 01:52:26,769
It was a box office hit, and was followed by a sequel, Drum (1976), which
starred Norton as a different character and Warren Oates as Hammond.

24
01:57:13,846 --> 01:57:19,846
The film explores themes of bare knuckle boxing, slavery,
interracial relationship, slave owner.

25
02:02:06,923 --> 02:02:12,923
The tone is emotional.
